  "description": " eggregate is a declared target here specifically as a CRASH GUARD. This fixture used to kill the eggregate process outright: egglog's Rust allocator called abort() during bounded saturation at bound 12, so the backend exited 134 with empty stdout \u2014 no envelope at all, which is the one result the five-outcome protocol has no home for. Because the fixture previously had no `expect.eggregate`, conformance never sent it there and the defect shipped unobserved. The expectation is deliberately the honest-inconclusive verdict rather than a grade: what is being guarded is that a well-formed GradeResponse comes back at all. NOTE: this row is slow (~75 s) \u2014 the escalating-bound search over a product of sums is genuinely expensive, which is the same property that made it explode."
